                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d53a410c-b090-4d58-85a5-675b2a56bd25",
                        "source_entry_id": "950b5c10-aabb-392f-aef7-cab024ae1b0e",
                        "source_sense_id": "4ac041f0-2d8b-3fb2-b327-d85b747b9bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "exhortation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exhortation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8d2daf2-ba15-3fe7-8f92-99af2af11834",
                                        "entry_id": "c8b4191e-85e8-3d0c-98ab-c670cd1ee183",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or practice of exhorting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09a869ff-68cf-40ab-8d71-3fee334bcee2",
                                                "sense_id": "d8d2daf2-ba15-3fe7-8f92-99af2af11834",
                                                "text": "All gladly drew round the table, and Mrs. Palmer's exhortation of “Poor dears, do enjoy yourselves,” was fulfilled, even to her own satisfaction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d5b15f3-51c9-40fd-87f5-76a79bb6f70b",
                                                "sense_id": "d8d2daf2-ba15-3fe7-8f92-99af2af11834",
                                                "text": "Earlier on the Other stage on Friday afternoon, Charli XCX took a more straightforward, rabble-rousing approach, a flurry of confetti cannon, inflatables and exhortations to wild hedonism: “I hope everyone gets really fucked up this weekend!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52d95a4b-6348-321c-9b2c-0843c9c08bfa",
                                        "entry_id": "c8b4191e-85e8-3d0c-98ab-c670cd1ee183",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Language intended to give advice or to urge or encourage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a26ab0ec-0519-400c-8050-39808cc559f3",
                                                "sense_id": "52d95a4b-6348-321c-9b2c-0843c9c08bfa",
                                                "text": "Come good Lorenzo, faryewell a while,\nIle end my exhortation after dinner."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e1f2547-8931-4e34-aead-24d6d01eb943",
                                                "sense_id": "52d95a4b-6348-321c-9b2c-0843c9c08bfa",
                                                "text": "And ye haue forgotten the exhortation which speaketh vnto you as vnto children, My sonne, despise not thou the chastening of the Lord, nor faint when thou art rebuked of him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf7b127c-09a6-48b2-822d-12ff77b0f62e",
                        "source_entry_id": "950b5c10-aabb-392f-aef7-cab024ae1b0e",
                        "source_sense_id": "4ac041f0-2d8b-3fb2-b327-d85b747b9bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "injunction",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "injunction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1839c0ff-5e87-3724-ab52-19071f8463e6",
                                        "entry_id": "7bf4663e-ec15-35ce-8671-db42fe142802",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of enjoining; the act of directing, commanding, or prohibiting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f797a81-ff31-3ab5-9854-3298b67c3b50",
                                        "entry_id": "7bf4663e-ec15-35ce-8671-db42fe142802",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which is enjoined; such as an order, mandate, decree, command, precept."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76b0dbe5-0e69-4459-ac12-47b4f76a16cd",
                                                "sense_id": "9f797a81-ff31-3ab5-9854-3298b67c3b50",
                                                "text": "[…]she added, “Lizzy, I insist upon your staying and hearing Mr. Collins.” Elizabeth would not oppose such an injunction—and a moment's consideration making her also sensible that it would be wisest to get it over as soon and as quietly as possible, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f094f104-e1e4-4df9-9bba-d360a56796e3",
                                                "sense_id": "9f797a81-ff31-3ab5-9854-3298b67c3b50",
                                                "text": "Its verbs are conjugated in a way that defies all the injunctions of the grammar books; it has its contumacious rules of tense, number and case; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da16c009-9388-4335-8845-57a071e40e55",
                                                "sense_id": "9f797a81-ff31-3ab5-9854-3298b67c3b50",
                                                "text": "At the end of the Falklands war two years earlier too, the Queen, whose second son, Andrew, had served as a helicopter pilot with the task force, was singularly untriumphalist and showed no inclination to follow her prime minister’s injunction to rejoice at victory."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81779dd2-7e01-3be4-82a2-c3f3b56cb787",
                                        "entry_id": "7bf4663e-ec15-35ce-8671-db42fe142802",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A writ or process, granted by a court of equity, and, in some cases, under statutes, by a court of law, whereby a party is required to do or to refrain from doing certain acts, according to the exigency of the writ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e18fec71-8ef4-460f-b34c-6d0a60c5a145",
                                                "sense_id": "81779dd2-7e01-3be4-82a2-c3f3b56cb787",
                                                "text": "Southwark council, which took out the injunction against Matt, believes YouTube has become the \"new playground\" for gang members."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46dd861b-9215-4cfa-86d1-e857724c4baa",
                                                "sense_id": "81779dd2-7e01-3be4-82a2-c3f3b56cb787",
                                                "text": "The judges said Trump must issue new orders reflecting the permanent injunction within 10 days."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "125eecf0-04d7-4cb6-b0b1-17f1846f81a5",
                        "source_entry_id": "950b5c10-aabb-392f-aef7-cab024ae1b0e",
                        "source_sense_id": "4ac041f0-2d8b-3fb2-b327-d85b747b9bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "rebuke",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rebuke",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "326db9cc-51a1-3ac3-b827-bad1463675a2",
                                        "entry_id": "7b8548d8-ca5f-34bb-b746-3daee1e92f89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A harsh criticism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61c1e58d-4ac0-4cc8-b3df-53e01971b6a7",
                                                "sense_id": "326db9cc-51a1-3ac3-b827-bad1463675a2",
                                                "text": "There was the sternness of an old-fashioned Tour patron in his rebuke to the young Frenchman Pierre Rolland, the only one to ride away from the peloton and seize the opportunity for a lone attack before being absorbed back into the bunch, where he was received with coolness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cc842e7-dd8c-48fe-bc7d-ee2ab9a774f4",
                                                "sense_id": "326db9cc-51a1-3ac3-b827-bad1463675a2",
                                                "text": "U.S. Vice President JD Vance met Saturday with the Vatican's No. 2 official, following a remarkable papal rebuke of the Trump administration’s crackdown on migrants and Vance’s theological justification of it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8e6cd1c-17dc-4750-9196-0aa247eeb4e6",
                                                "sense_id": "326db9cc-51a1-3ac3-b827-bad1463675a2",
                                                "text": "With his emphasis on accepting the science (he was a trained chemist) – and hence his stern rebuke to the climate change deniers and the politicians who courted them – he even managed to reset the relationship between science and religion, which had been rocky ever since Galileo fell foul of the Inquisition 400 years earlier."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rebuke",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3daaaf7d-cae5-3236-b6b0-027d2e58743e",
                                        "entry_id": "85a7cc07-1d91-36da-a09f-c49cb5120dd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To criticise harshly; to reprove."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d18bd88-1267-4e59-9a2f-1c9c46d83083",
                                                "sense_id": "3daaaf7d-cae5-3236-b6b0-027d2e58743e",
                                                "text": "O Lord, do not rebuke me in Your anger or discipline me in Your wrath."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9dba2392-0010-46fb-8295-9bbb7acbb938",
                        "source_entry_id": "950b5c10-aabb-392f-aef7-cab024ae1b0e",
                        "source_sense_id": "4ac041f0-2d8b-3fb2-b327-d85b747b9bfa",
                        "target_lang_word": "chastisement",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chastisement",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                        "entry_id": "fd09b30f-74c4-3936-9029-e7e9fe370c7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of chastising; rebuke; punishment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b26656f-31fa-4604-b28b-0f74c74541c2",
                                                "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                                "text": "Besides, the King hath wasted all his rods\nOn late offenders, that he now doth lack\nThe very instruments of chastisement;\nSo that his power, like to a fangless lion,\nMay offer, but not hold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fda40b6-43bf-4446-84d3-7e11f4b7f526",
                                                "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                                "text": "But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ced9c07-f9da-407c-9997-15aab41562d4",
                                                "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                                "text": "All this he called “doing his duty by their parents;” and he never inflicted a chastisement without following it by the assurance, so consolatory to the smarting urchin, that “he would remember it and thank him for it the longest day he had to live.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98d7b283-8919-4018-8a43-4ca5a874e74a",
                                                "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                                "text": "Into the details of the infamy at which I thus connived (for even now I can scarce grant that I committed it) I have no design of entering; I mean but to point out the warnings and the successive steps with which my chastisement approached."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f93e3b7-c5a6-436d-8e0b-2759b21bae78",
                                                "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                                "text": "It seems to me that as he does not respond to this extremely conciliatory treatment it may be well to try whether a change of treatment might not produce a more satisfactory result. If praise and courtesy only result in narrow, bitter partisanship, perhaps a little well-merited chastisement may procure some geniality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c74a7215-f9ad-4aa1-97ee-5fa01375985d",
                                                "sense_id": "8db3dcf5-931c-39d8-b6de-47e92f9a9e57",
                                                "text": "Abolition of defence of reasonable chastisement"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
